  "reasoning": "The defendant operated two hot‑pot restaurants and sold large quantities of meat that was past its expiration date. The sale of expired food that does not meet safety standards constitutes the crime of producing and selling food that is not in compliance with safety standards under Chinese criminal law. No other distinct criminal conduct (e.g., fraud, theft) is described. Therefore the appropriate charge is the food‑safety offense.",
  "final_answer": "[罪名]生产、销售不符合安全标准的食品<eoa>"
